  <p>
    Zag.js splits every UI machine into two halves: a framework-agnostic state machine
    (<code>packages/core</code>) and a thin per-framework binding layer
    (<code>packages/frameworks/*</code>) that turns that machine into idiomatic, reactive
    framework code. This document is a reverse-engineered reference for what that binding layer
    — the &quot;adapter&quot; — must implement, built entirely from reading the adapter source
    trees, never from prior assumptions.
